{"kind":"artifact","text":"Candidate at performance for the retained fan-out evidence, exact head fd513938b257a83cc998d9fea7cefdf3543198b3.\n\nWHAT CHANGED HERE. Two things, both under performance. A new tracked directory performance/retained/fanout-20260819-f71b4d73 holding exactly three files, and a rewritten retention section in performance/README.md. performance/.gitignore is untouched: its diff against main is empty, which I verified rather than assumed.\n\nWHY. A run writes into performance/evidence, which is ignored working space inside the worktree, and step 6 of the working discipline deletes that worktree after merge. The previous fan-out campaign went that way. Its three digests are still quoted in the log and its page still told readers the medians must not replace the distributions, but the distributions were gone. This retains the run the published verdict actually cites, before the same thing can happen to it.\n\nTHE THREE FILES, and only three. evidence.json 61a53e96c9bf31da07d7e37722d5bd2225f4f5ea9dad5a8bbf2e30acf9254a7b, samples.jsonl 21c74a93ff7ec928297b4fb25196244d1c61529b60b8028abe27f3d1f8ff3209, candidate.bench f5078a0e1263305c3615359c7f558c9ed12df414c3b5fe4da74afd28aa9e93e6. I recomputed all three at this head. git ls-files performance/retained returns exactly these and nothing else.\n\nNothing derived is retained. An earlier version of this work also tracked a notes file, a distributions file and the machine load log; review found that beyond the authorization, and it was right on the merits as well as the scope. evidence.json already carries the contract, environment, fixture and contract digests and the exact head, and every distribution, median and increment is recomputable from the samples, so a stored copy of derived numbers is one more thing that can drift from the data it describes. What those files did carry that mattered was the account of how the run was conducted, and that has moved into docs/reference/performance.md where it is reviewed rather than sitting unread beside the data. Profiles, traces and fixtures are excluded: the first two are diagnostic reruns rather than primary evidence, and fixtures are large and regenerable from the contract.\n\nSECURITY. I scanned all three files for absolute local paths, the operator's username, private key blocks, and password or secret-key strings. Zero hits in each. Nothing in this change touches signing, admission, verification, fold semantics or publication; it adds data files and prose.\n\nTHE RUN THESE FILES RECORD. Measured at f71b4d73, an ancestor of this head, contract digest b0795bc7 recomputed independently, one fixture exact digest d15f714d throughout, clean worktree, Darwin arm64 on an 18-core Apple M5 Max, Go 1.26.5, Git 2.50.1. 505 records: 100 primary samples per width at 1, 8, 16, 64 and 256, plus one round-zero diagnostic each. All 500 primary trusted-versus-projected digest pairs equal, checked by me. One process invocation, exit 0.\n\nTWO FACTS ABOUT ITS CONDUCT, now carried by the page rather than by a note here. It is a second attempt: an earlier invocation was suspended by machine sleep 48 samples in, and because sample records carry no wall-clock timestamp a spanning suspend cannot be found afterwards in the data, so the run was discarded whole rather than partly repaired. And the quiet window did not hold: a sibling lane started two test processes a minute into measurement, load peaked at 14.53, and width one, which runs first and is the sole denominator, absorbed it.\n\nMECHANISM. Retention stays a deliberate act on one run whose numbers reach a page, not an automatic consequence of running the harness. The ignore rules are unchanged, so a run is copied out of ignored space before review, and README.md now describes that and the three-file policy instead of the wider set it briefly promised.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD. go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 26 packages, zero failures, docset uncached at 63.293 seconds. gofmt clean, working tree clean. Pushed; merge-base with origin/main is 92dd2df1 itself.\n\nPredecessor at this path is 4da5ebd0, live and not stale when I checked immediately before publishing. Retirement belongs to the merge, not here. I have not merged.","body":{"commit":"fd513938b257a83cc998d9fea7cefdf3543198b3","path":"performance"}}